| counts_gene | 01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv |

## Method
1. Load gene counts matrix and sample metadata from the design file (01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk_design.csv) using R in the gars-bio conda environment.
2. Apply log2 transformation with pseudocount (log2(counts + 1)) to stabilize variance across the range of expression values.
3. Compute PCA on the log-transformed counts using the base R prcomp() function, scaling features to unit variance.
4. Extract PCA coordinates for PC1 and PC2, which together typically capture the dominant sources of variation.
5. Generate a scatter plot using ggplot2 with points colored by the condition column from metadata (untreated: one color, treated: another), with PC1 and PC2 as axes. Add sample labels.
6. Report the percentage of variance explained by each of the first five principal components.
7. Write results to results/pca_scores.csv (sample coordinates and PC values) and results/pca_variance.txt (variance explained per PC), and the plot to results/pca_plot.pdf.

